{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "PHP Superglobals"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use these words to talk about Superglobals."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.\t Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Perfect Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Past perfect</strong> is used for an action that happened before another."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we talk about events in the past, some actions happened before than others, for those older sentences, we use <strong>past perfect.</strong><br/><br/>Look at the following structure:<br/><br><center>Subject + <b>had </b>+ <b>verb in past participle</b> + complement</center><br/><br/>Examples<br/><span class=\"italic\">When he created the all Superglobal codes, the developers <b>had installed</b> a faster program. </span><br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">Before I presented the exam about Superglobals, the teacher <b>had already explained </b>their functions. </span><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Only a bunch of people had been capable of working in software "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The software developers had worked tirelessly and non-stop until Superglobals made it easier. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Wish + Past Form of Verb for Wishes \u2013 Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>wish + negative past form of verbs</strong> to express that we would like things to be different."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Wish + negative past form of verbs</strong> helps us to express that we don't like the way things are.<br/><br/>Look at the following structure:<br/>Subject + <b>wish</b> + subject + negative past form of verb + complement<br/><br/>Examples<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <b>wish </b>Jenny <b>didn't damage </b>all the codes.<br/>I <b>wish</b> you <b>didn't have</b> a lot of problems with the Superglobals.<br/>The developer <b>wishes</b> the programmer<b> weren't</b> too delayed in his job. <br/><br> Remember that you use the plural form  of verb to be ( were/ weren't) after wish  because it's subjuntive and more formal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I could bet you wish programming language weren't so difficult.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You wish you didn't have to study so many variables, right?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bunch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of, few"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Only a bunch of people had been capable of working in software."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "include "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take into account, to have inside it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The introduction of Superglobals. They included them since PHP version 4.1.0."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "built-in "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "included in a machine or product"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can consider them as built-in variables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "effort "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of energy and time something takes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are available and can be accessible from any function, class or even file without any effort! It saves time and energy"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tirelessly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without rest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The software developers had worked tirelessly until Superglobals made it easier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get familiarized "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to learn a lot about something and be comfortable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When you start to get familiarized with it, you will love it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for a complete list of superglobals in PHP."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a chart where you include the superglobals and their characteristics.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a presentation with the most common parameters. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your presentation with the class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify superglobals in PHP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list superglobals. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand the characteristics of superglobals.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with the class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "I could bet you wish programming language weren't so difficult. Decades ago, only a bunch of people had been capable of working in software, but all the progress we have had is making the software language and programming friendlier.</br>\nLet's talk about one of those huge progress tolls; that one is the introduction of Superglobals. They included them since PHP version 4.1.0. You can consider them as built-in variables. What every programmer loves about them is the fact that they are available and can be accessible from any function, class or even file without any effort! It saves time and energy.</br>"}, {"time": "47000", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "The software developers had worked tirelessly and non-stop until Superglobals made it easier. There is a total of nine Superglobals, they are:</br></br>$GLOBALS</br>\n$_SERVER</br>\n$_REQUEST</br>\n$_POST</br>\n$_GET</br>\n$_FILES</br>\n$_ENV</br>\n$_COOKIE</br>\n$_SESSION</br></br>You wish you didn't have to study so many variables, right? Don't worry; we will just study some of them in this lesson.</br></br>Let's start with $GLOBALS, they are used to access global variables from anywhere in the script! Pretty amazing, don't you think so? This is possible because PHP stores all the global variables in a special array or index. When you start to get familiarized with it, you will love it.</br></br>"}, {"time": "117000", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "$_SERVER is our second superglobal, it stores not variables but rather the information about headers, paths, and script locations.</br></br>$_REQUEST, $_POST,  and $_GET are all used to collect data after submitting the HTLM form, they have some differences, and the uses differ according to your needs, but we will work on that later on, just remember what they do in general terms.</br></br>Let's finish today lesson with that. I know you are excited, and you wish we didn't have to wait until next week to continue on this topic, but for now, just study these Superglobals by your own.</br></br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n6le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what superglobals in PHP are.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list superglobals in PHP.   "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about characteristics of some superglobals in PHP. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the advantages of Superglobals?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think we always need to use them? Explain."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "G